name 'aif-y2-ai-at-scale-postassessment-q12-2026'

wrong 'The network hasn\’t trained long enough, and more training iterations would eventually fix the predictions.'
wrong 'Temperature and plant growth aren\’t related, so no model could learn a useful pattern from this data.'
wrong 'The temperature weight is too small, and a larger weight would let the network fit the data.'
right 'A single-layer network\’s output can only move in one direction as an input increases.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

markdown <<MARKDOWN
A student wants to predict how much a plant will grow based on the temperature. Plants in the training data grow best around 75°F and grow less when it’s either colder or hotter. The student trains a neural network with no hidden layers, but its predictions are poor no matter how long it trains. Which statement best explains why?
MARKDOWN

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 9: What Neurons Learn
MARKDOWN
